# Bucketeer SwiftFormat config — sanity gate, not a style
# enforcer. The repo already converged on its own hand-written
# conventions (variable-aligned columns, informal line lengths,
# explicit multi-line lists); applying SwiftFormat's full ruleset
# would mass-rewrite ~85% of the codebase for cosmetic-only
# reasons.
#
# Instead we run a *deny everything by default, allow a tiny set
# of objectively-correct rules* policy. Every rule listed here
# catches a real bug a human reviewer would also flag. Add more
# only after a coordinated cleanup pass for that specific rule
# across the existing codebase.

--swiftversion 6.0
--indent 4
--self init-only

# Allow-list: only these rules fire.
--rules linebreakAtEndOfFile,trailingSpace,duplicateImports,redundantBackticks,redundantBreak
